API Design Notes
The API follows a consistent structure for creating tasks.
project_id identifies the project that will contain the task.
title is required.
description is optional.
assignee_id identifies the user assigned to the task.
due_date specifies the task deadline.
priority must be low, medium, or high.
Authentication is required.
A successful task creation returns 201 Created.
The API uses JSON for request and response bodies.
The task ID is generated by the server.
The response provides information about the newly created task.
Conclusion
This technical writing lab demonstrates two important forms of software documentation.
The User Manual Procedure focuses on helping beginner users complete a technical task through clear prerequisites, individual actions, expected results, screenshots, and troubleshooting information.
The API Reference Entry provides developers with the technical information required to use an API endpoint correctly, including the HTTP method, endpoint path, parameters, authentication, request body, response codes, and JSON examples.
Both forms of documentation should be clear, accurate, consistent, and appropriate for their intended audience.

